### Livewire Components
- Create modular, reusable Livewire components.
- Use Livewire’s lifecycle hooks effectively (e.g., mount, updated).
- Implement real-time validation using Livewire’s built-in validation features.
- Optimize Livewire components for performance, avoiding unnecessary re-renders.
- Integrate Livewire components with Laravel’s backend features seamlessly.
- Implement lazy loading for Livewire components when appropriate.

### Patient Management (e.g., PatientManager)
- Implement patient management features: create/edit patient cards (name, phone, email, notes), manage patient communications (messages, appointment requests), and add patient-specific notes.
- Use Livewire for dynamic patient lists and forms, ensuring real-time updates.
- Integrate with Eloquent models (e.g., Patient, Vitrin) for data consistency.
- Display patients in card format with TailwindCSS, ensuring responsive design.

### Appointment Scheduling (e.g., VisibilityManager)
- Implement appointment scheduling: manage available time slots (e.g., JSON format: {"Monday": ["09:00-10:00"]}).
- Allow visibility settings (e.g., toggle listing on hekimport.com).
- Use Livewire for dynamic slot management (add/remove slots).
- Ensure user-friendly UI with TailwindCSS, including clear labels and responsive layout.

### Blade Templating and Alpine.js
- Use Laravel’s Blade templating engine for views, integrating with Livewire, Alpine.js, and FilamentPHP.
- Use Alpine.js directives (x-data, x-bind, x-on, etc.) for declarative JavaScript functionality.
- Implement small, focused Alpine.js components for specific UI interactions (e.g., modals, toggles).
- Combine Alpine.js with Livewire for enhanced interactivity when necessary.
- Keep Alpine.js logic close to the HTML it manipulates, preferably inline.

### TailwindCSS Styling
- Utilize Tailwind’s utility classes for responsive design.
- Implement a consistent color scheme (#00c8b3 to #0099e5 gradient) and typography (Orbitron for headings, Inter for body) using Tailwind’s configuration.
- Use Tailwind’s @apply directive in CSS files for reusable component styles (e.g., .btn-gradient, .card-hover).
- Optimize for production by purging unused CSS classes.
- Add subtle animations (e.g., hover effects, transitions) for a modern, creative vibe.
- Ensure all UI elements (e.g., cards, buttons, forms) are responsive and mobile-friendly.
- Apply hover effects (e.g., transform: scale, shadow changes) to interactive elements like buttons and cards.

### FilamentPHP Integration
- Leverage FilamentPHP for admin panels (e.g., Masam dashboard) and widgets (e.g., analytics dashboards, form builders).
- Ensure seamless integration with Laravel and Livewire for dynamic, user-friendly interfaces.
- Create reusable FilamentPHP widgets for analytics (e.g., visits, clicks, impressions) in the Vitrin Analizim section.
- Style FilamentPHP components with TailwindCSS, matching the project’s aesthetic (#00c8b3 to #0099e5 gradient, Orbitron/Inter fonts).
- Use FilamentPHP tables for displaying analytics data, with filtering and sorting capabilities.
- Integrate with Eloquent models (e.g., VitrinAnalytic) for data consistency.